# Normalize everything to LF in the repo and on checkout, except Windows scripts.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Golden scene fixtures are compared BYTE-FOR-BYTE by tests/scene_serialize_test.cpp and
# tests/editor/scene_golden_test.cpp (task 2.5.2). The blanket `* text=auto eol=lf` above already
# covers them; this line is explicit so narrowing that rule cannot silently break the comparison on
# Windows, where a CRLF checkout would make every fixture fail with a hygiene complaint.
*.scene.json text eol=lf
# The phase-1 sample is byte-compared too (G9, AC-13) but is named `scene.json`, which `*.scene.json`
# does NOT match -- verified with `git check-attr text eol`. It needs its own line for the sentence
# above to be true of every file the batteries compare.
samples/phase-1-scene/scene.json text eol=lf

# Golden project fixtures are compared BYTE-FOR-BYTE by tests/editor/project_test.cpp (task 2.6.1),
# and New Project writes real `project.json` files into test temp directories whose bytes the same
# battery compares. TWO patterns are required, not one: `*.project.json` does NOT match a bare
# `project.json` -- the identical glob trap recorded above for samples/phase-1-scene/scene.json, and
# verified the same way, with `git check-attr text eol`.
*.project.json text eol=lf
project.json   text eol=lf

# Golden asset-meta fixtures are compared BYTE-FOR-BYTE by tests/editor/asset_meta_test.cpp
# (task 3.1.1), and the database writes real .meta files into test temp directories whose bytes the
# same battery compares. Unlike *.scene.json / *.project.json, ONE pattern suffices: `*.meta`
# matches both `minimal.meta` and `wood.png.meta`. Verify with `git check-attr text eol -- <path>`.
*.meta text eol=lf

# Binary asset types (extended as asset work lands in Phase 3+)
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ktx2 binary
*.glb binary
